+# S004 Retry-credit data model
+
+## WorkspaceRetryQuota
+
+One current quota record per workspace.
+
+| Field | Purpose | Rules |
+|---|---|---|
+| `workspace_id` | quota owner | Primary/unique key; all operations scope to it. |
+| `available_credits` | credits that may be reserved | Non-negative integer enforced by the database. |
+| `updated_at` | accounting audit point | Updated in each quota-mutating transaction. |
+
+The configured quota capacity is outside this story. This story only reserves from and restores to `available_credits`.
+
+## RetryCreditReservation
+
+One durable accounting record per logical provider send attempt.
+
+| Field | Purpose | Rules |
+|---|---|---|
+| `id` | reservation identity | Primary key. |
+| `workspace_id` | quota owner | References `WorkspaceRetryQuota`. |
+| `attempt_key` | stable logical send-attempt identity | Unique with `workspace_id`; reused for retry-safe reservation and callback settlement. |
+| `state` | lifecycle | `reserved`, `finalized`, or `released`. |
+| `provider_reference` | optional provider correlation | Nullable; never required to settle by `attempt_key`. |
+| `reserved_at` | reservation audit point | Set once at creation. |
+| `settled_at` | terminal audit point | Set only on first terminal transition. |
+| `settlement_reason` | outcome audit value | `accepted`, `failed`, `timed_out`, or `cancelled`; immutable once terminal. |
+
+## State transitions
+
+```text
+reserve:     (no reservation) -> reserved    [decrement available_credits atomically]
+accept:      reserved -> finalized           [no credit restoration]
+release:     reserved -> released            [increment available_credits atomically]
+duplicate:   finalized/released -> same state [no quota mutation]
+```
+
+`finalized` and `released` are terminal. A conflicting later callback is not permitted to alter accounting; it must return the recorded terminal state and be observable to operations.
+
+## Integrity rules
+
+1. `available_credits >= 0` is enforced at storage level.
+2. `(workspace_id, attempt_key)` is unique.
+3. Reservation creation and quota decrement are one transaction.
+4. Release state change and quota increment are one transaction.
+5. Settlement updates require `state = reserved`; a zero-row conditional update means the callback is a duplicate or conflict and must not mutate quota.
