+# S004 Manual validation quickstart
+
+## Preconditions
+
+1. Create a workspace with a known `available_credits` balance.
+2. Configure a controllable provider test double that can accept, fail, time out, or be cancelled.
+3. Record the logical `attempt_key` for each send.
+
+## Scenarios
+
+| Scenario | Action | Expected result |
+|---|---|---|
+| Accepted send | Begin a send with one available credit; have the provider accept it. | Balance decreases by one; reservation is `finalized`; a repeated accepted callback changes nothing. |
+| Provider failure | Begin a send; have the provider fail. | Balance returns to its pre-send value; reservation is `released`; a repeated failure callback changes nothing. |
+| Timeout | Begin a send; force a timeout. | Balance returns once; reservation is `released` with `timed_out`. |
+| Cancellation | Begin a send; cancel before acceptance. | Balance returns once; reservation is `released` with `cancelled`. |
+| Exhaustion | Set balance to zero and begin a send. | Reservation is rejected and the provider is not called. |
+| Concurrent sends | Set balance to one; begin two distinct attempts concurrently. | Exactly one reserves and sends; the other is rejected; balance never becomes negative. |
+| Duplicate/mixed callback | Deliver the same terminal callback twice, then a conflicting callback. | First terminal state stays authoritative; no extra charge or release occurs; conflict is observable. |
+
+## Automated evidence to retain
+
+- Unit tests for each legal and duplicate state transition.
+- Integration test proving concurrent reservation safety against the real transaction mechanism.
+- Integration tests for provider acceptance, failure, timeout, cancellation, and repeated callbacks.
